  "notes": "Used across multiple contexts: postal mail, email, phone calls, and digital data.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- メールを{転送|てんそう}する (to forward an email)\n- {電話|でんわ}を{転送|てんそう}する (to transfer a call)\n- {郵便|ゆうびん}{転送|てんそう} (mail forwarding)\n- {自動|じどう}{転送|てんそう} (auto-forwarding)\n- データを{転送|てんそう}する (to transfer data)\n\nUSAGE:\nFor postal mail, the Japan Post Office offers a free {転送|てんそう} service that redirects mail from your old address to your new one for one year after moving. This is a very common practical use of the word.",
